issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.7.stable.mono.official [5b4e0cb0f]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA RTX 500 Ada Generation Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9647) - Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 7 155H (22 threads) - 31.50 GiB memory - WASAPI (96000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nChanging a built-in `BoxContainer` from vertical to horizontal can leave nested container contents with stale dimensions when the children are `PanelContainer`s using a `StyleBoxTexture` with non-zero texture margins.\n\nAfter changing `BoxContainer.vertical`, the `PanelContainer` and `MarginContainer` are resized correctly, but the nested `HBoxContainer` may retain its previous width. This causes an expanding `Label` to place the following `TextureRect` outside the panel bounds.\n\nThe issue still occurs when the `StyleBoxTexture` content margins are explicitly set to `0`. Removing the texture margins prevents it.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the attached reproduction project.\n2. Run the scene.\n3. Press the button to switch the `BoxContainer` from horizontal to vertical and back.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAll nested containers are laid out correctly, and the icon remains inside the `PanelContainer`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe nested `HBoxContainer` retains a stale width, causing the icon to overflow the panel.\n\n### Workaround\n\nManually queueing and awaiting `SortChildren` for each nested container fixes the layout.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[box-container-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30015336/box-container-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121372/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121372/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}